tongue up, out through the nose (sing)"}],"audio":[{"src":"audio/Vv4.mp3","label":"聽 · synthetic","real":false,"voice":"female"}]},{"id":"v5","en":"to say, to speak","note":"","cells":[{"ch":"說","py":"shuō","t":1,"s":"说","mk":["p2","2","#C92A2A"]}],"cues":[{"sym":"2","col":"#C92A2A","lab":"sh","cue":"Position 2: tip up · shi ≈ ‘shrr’","kind":"p2"}],"audio":[{"src":"audio/Vv5.mp3","label":"說 · synthetic","real":false,"voice":"female"}]},{"id":"v6","en":"to be able to","note":"learned ability (‘know how to’)","cells":[{"ch":"會","py":"huì","t":4,"s":"会","fc":[["ei","ten-E: ei like ‘vein’"],["u(e)i","hidden vowel: -ui = u(e)i, -iu = i(o)u, -un = u(e)n"]]}],"cues":[{"chip":"ei","lab":"huì","cue":"ei like ‘vein’"},{"chip":"u(e)i","lab":"huì","cue":"-ui = u(e)i, -iu = i(o)u, -un = u(e)n"}],"audio":[{"src":"audio/Vv6.mp3","label":"會 · synthetic","real":false,"voice":"female"}]},{"id":"v7","en":"not","note":"→ bú before a 4th (assertive): bú huì","cells":[{"ch":"不","py":"bù","t":4,"mk":["nopuff","°","#E67700"]}],"cues":[{"sym":"°","col":"#E67700","lab":"b","cue":"no puff, no voice: sPin","kind":"nopuff"}],"audio":[{"src":"audio/Vv7.mp3","label":"不 · synthetic","real":false,"voice":"female"}]},{"id":"v8","en":"Mandarin / Chinese language","note":"","cells":[{"ch":"中","py":"zhōng","t":1,"mk":["p2","2","#C92A2A"]},{"ch":"文","py":"wén","t":2,"fc":[["-n","-n: tip ends on the ridge behind top teeth (ban)"],["e = uh","short-E: en/eng ≈ quick ‘uh’ (ba-NA-na)"]]}],"cues":[{"chip":"-n","lab":"wén","cue":"tip ends on the ridge behind top teeth (ban)"},{"chip":"e = uh","lab":"wén","cue":"en/eng ≈ quick ‘uh’ (ba-NA-na)"}],"audio":[{"src":"audio/Vv8.mp3","label":"中文 · synthetic","real":false,"voice":"female"}]},{"id":"v9","en":"[question]","note":"yes/no particle; contrarian (neutral) tone","cells":[{"ch":"嗎","py":"ma","t":5,"s":"吗"}],"cues":[],"audio":[{"src":"audio/Vv9.mp3","label":"嗎 · synthetic","real":false,"voice":"female"}]},{"id":"v10","en":"a little","note":"said yìdiǎn; 一點點 = ‘a tiny bit’","cells":[{"ch":"一","py":"yī","t":1,"mk":["yi","↗","#17A398"],"said":"yì"},{"ch":"點","py":"diǎn","t":3,"s":"点","mk":["nopuff","°","#E67700"]}],"cues":[{"sym":"↗","col":"#17A398","lab":"yī diǎn","cue":"yī → yì before a 3rd","kind":"yi"}],"audio":[{"src":"audio/Vv10.mp3","label":"一點 · synthetic","real":false,"voice":"female"}]},{"id":"v11","en":"correct / right","note":"","cells":[{"ch":"對","py":"duì","t":4,"s":"对"}],"cues":[],"audio":[{"src":"audio/Vv11.mp3","label":"對 · synthetic","real":false,"voice":"female"}]},{"id":"v12","en":"[suggestion]","note":"here: seeks agreement (‘…, right?’)","cells":[{"ch":"吧","py":"ba","t":5}],"cues":[],"audio":[{"src":"audio/Vv12.mp3","label":"吧 · synthetic","real":false,"voice":"female"}]},{"id":"v13","en":"English language","note":"","cells":[{"ch":"英","py":"yīng","t":1},{"ch":"文","py":"wén","t":2}],"cues":[],"audio":[{"src":"audio/Vv13.mp3","label":"英文 · synthetic","real":false,"voice":"female"}]},{"id":"v14","en":"Good luck! / You got this!","note":"lit. ‘add oil’","cells":[{"ch":"加","py":"jiā","t":1,"mk":["p1","1","#C92A2A"]},{"ch":"油","py":"yóu","t":2}],"cues":[{"sym":"1","col":"#C92A2A","lab":"j","cue":"Position 1: tip behind bottom teeth","kind":"p1"}],"audio":[{"src":"audio/Vv14.mp3","label":"加油 · synthetic","real":false,"voice":"female"}]}]},{"type":"cards","title":"Listening notes","items":[["The zombie 3rd is the default.","Of 17 3rd-tone tokens, 10 are MB’s zombie (low 21 ˨˩, no rise) before another tone, 3 undergo 3+3 (你好 ×2, 點點), and only the 4 phrase-final ones (好, 點) can show the full 214 — often still low. Aim low, not for the rise."],["3+3 → 2+3 in 你好 and 一點點.","Two zombies in a row: the first turns unsure (rising). nǐ hǎo is said ní hǎo; in yì diǎn diǎn the first diǎn rises. The published pinyin keeps dictionary marks, so the change is audible but not written. Likewise bù → bú (×3), yī → yì (×2)."],["Two kinds of yes/no question.","你會說中文嗎？ is marked by the particle; 你不會？ has no particle — expect a raised pitch range on the final huì while its fall is kept (intonation is layered on tone, it doesn’t replace it)."],["Interjections are intonational.","呃 È and 喔 Ō are drawn with the tones in the official pinyin, but their pitch follows discourse, not the lexicon — treat those contours as a guide only and copy the audio."],["Listen for regional cues.","Traditional script, 喔, and 一點點 without 兒 hint at a Taiwan-style norm: do 中/說 use MB’s Position 2 (retroflex [ʈʂ ʂ]) or drift toward Position 3 z/s [ts s]? Note: no erhua."]]}],"schema":1,"date":"2026-10-11T08:00-04:00"}